@3. Command reference
.
=3. COMMAND REFERENCE
.
.40 keywords, encoded $CE7F down to $CE4D and allocated downward. Eleven of
.the fifty-one slots are holes and stay holes: the byte values are the ABI
.and are never renumbered.
.
=At a glance -- where each part comes from
.
.Three implementations, and what each costs:
.
.  - ASM -- a keyword run by machine code in the runtime. Costs runtime
.    bytes, and one GP keyword anywhere in a program pays for the whole
.    1,536-byte block. Documented in SEC 3.
.  - BASIC -- a .INC.BL module of ordinary BASL, called with GOSUB. Costs
.    nothing unless #INCLUDEd, and then only its own p-code. Documented in
.    SEC 4.
.  - COMPOSITE -- a keyword with no machine code of its own; the compiler
.    expands it into keywords that already exist. Costs the runtime nothing.
.    Documented in SEC 3 with the ASM keywords.
.
.  Loops
.      ASM
.      GP.DO GP.LOOP GP.EXITDO
.
.  Multi-way branch
.      ASM
.      GP.SELECT GP.CASE GP.OTHER GP.ENDSEL
.
.  Block IF
.      ASM
.      GP.IF GP.ELSEIF GP.ELSE GP.ENDIF -- see SEC 3.8
.
.  Machine code
.      ASM
.      GP.CALL GP.A GP.X GP.Y GP.C
.
.  Inline assembly
.      COMPOSITE
.      GP.ASM GP.ENDASM -- free, and leaves the block out, see SEC 3.9
.
.  Strings
.      ASM
.      GP.INSTR GP.STRPTR GP.COMP
.
.  Strings
.      COMPOSITE
.      GP.CONTAINS GP.ISEMPTY -- free, see SEC 3.4
.
.  Addresses
.      COMPOSITE
.      GP.HIBYTE GP.LOBYTE -- free, see SEC 3.3.1
.
.  Arrays
.      ASM
.      GP.ARRPTR
.
.  Banked text
.      ASM
.      GP.BANKEDSTR GP.ENDBANKEDSTR GP.BSTR GP.BSTRSET - GP.BSTRCOUNT is
.        COMPOSITE -- see SEC 3.10
.
.  Routine calls
.      COMPOSITE
.      GP.DEFPROC GP.SUB -- free, and leaves the block out, see SEC 3.11
.
.  Routine calls
.      ASM
.      GP.FN -- the same call as a value, and it brings the GP block in
.
.  Screen
.      ASM
.      GP.BOX GP.FILL GP.PRINTAT
.
.  Screen
.      COMPOSITE
.      GP.CHAR -- free, one cell in GP.PRINTAT's shape running GP.FILL's
.        handler
.
.  Colour roles
.      BASIC
.      THEME.INC.BL -- THEME.SELECT, THEME.CLR() - SEC 4.1
.
.  String helpers
.      BASIC+ASM
.      STRINGS.INC.BL -- PADR PADL PADC SPLIT REPLACE SPLICE PET2SCR TRIM
.        LTRIM RTRIM - SEC 4.2
.
.  Screen etiquette, panels
.      BASIC
.      APPSYS.INC.BL -- STARTUP RESTORE PANEL.SAVE/LOAD/PUT ISEMU - SEC 4.3
.
.  Entry fields
.      BASIC
.      LINEINPUT.INC.BL -- LINEINPUT.GET, LINEINPUT.ASK - SEC 4.4
.
.  Bitmaps
.      BASIC+ASM
.      BMX.INC.BL -- BMX.OPEN PAINT SHOW CLOSE RESTORE, BMX.LOAD a verb - SEC
.        4.5
.
.  Menus
.      BASIC
.      MENU.INC.BL -- MENU.BEGIN ITEM ITEMX SELECTED DRAWBAR, MENUTO.VERT
.        MENUTO.BAR - SEC 4.6
.
.  Menus
.      BASIC
.      MENUPULL.INC.BL -- MENUTO.PULLDOWN, a dropdown under a bar item - SEC
.        4.9
.
.  Dialogs
.      BASIC
.      GUI.INC.BL -- GUI.SAY GUI.YN GUI.MENU GUI.INPUT GUI.OPEN GUI.CLOSE -
.        SEC 4.11
.
.  Dialogs
.      BASIC
.      GUI-DIALOGS.INC.BL -- every dialog as a one-line verb - SEC 4.12
.
.  Dialogs
.      BASIC
.      COMBO.INC.BL -- COMBO.ADD, a drop-down that folds into one row - SEC
.        4.17
.
.  Dialogs
.      BASIC
.      CHECK.INC.BL -- CHECK.ADD, a check box, [X] or [ ] - SEC 4.21
.
.  Dialogs
.      BASIC
.      GUI-LITE.INC.BL -- MSGBOX PICKMENU CLOSEBOX, in low memory, nothing
.        banked - SEC 4.24
.
.  Code in a bank
.      ASM
.      GP.BANKED GP.ENDBANKED -- p-code at $A000, out of the low-memory
.        budget, see SEC 3.12
.
.  Bank ownership
.      BASIC
.      BANKMGR.INC.BL -- INIT CLAIM GET.FREE.BANK RELEASE COUNT - SEC 4.13
.
.  Key-value store
.      BASIC
.      KV.INC.BL -- INIT GET PUT DEL FIND AT WIPE SAVE LOAD, strings in one
.        RAM bank - SEC 4.20
.
.  Key-value store
.      BASIC
.      KVBIN.INC.BL -- CREATE INFO GET PUT DEL AT FIRST NEXT STOP EXPAND,
.        strings in one file that every program shares - SEC 4.26
.
.  Keyboard
.      BASIC
.      KB.INC.BL -- KB.CLEARKB - SEC 4.14
.
.  The drive
.      BASIC
.      FILEIO.INC.BL -- STATUS EXISTS SIZE DELETE RENAME COPY MKDIR CHDIR
.        SAVEARRAY LOADARRAY - SEC 4.15
.
.  The drive
.      BASIC
.      FILEDIR.INC.BL -- FILE.DIR.INIT OPEN NEXT, into a bank or low RAM -
.        SEC 4.16
.
.  The drive
.      BASIC
.      DOS.INC.BL -- DOSX DOSX.EXISTS, the smaller alternative to FILEIO -
.        SEC 4.25
.
.  Screen -- stash
.      BASIC
.      STASHVRAM.INC.BL -- SV.SAVE SV.RESTORE SV.PUT SV.GET, kept in VRAM -
.        SEC 4.18
.
.  Screen -- stash
.      BASIC
.      STASHVRAMGC.INC.BL -- SV.COMPACT - SEC 4.19
.
.  Numbers
.      BASIC
.      MATH.INC.BL -- MATH.MIN MATH.MAX - SEC 4.22
.
.  Memory
.      BASIC
.      MEM.INC.BL -- MEM.COPY MEM.FILL, the KERNAL's block move - SEC 4.23
.
.The rule is in SEC 1: assembly for tight loops and bulk data moves, BASIC
.for everything else, and a composite for anything that is only a spelling of
.keywords already present.
.
.The keywords in detail. Square brackets mean optional. Optionals cannot be
.skipped over: GP.BOX X,Y,W,H,,7 is a syntax error -- write out the default
.you are passing through.
.
